{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "a99521fa-5728-8bb7-9ba3-aa8c8bccb658",
  "created_at": "2026-02-05T11:51:36-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Stephen Sisson",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Lorraine Medeiros",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:49:38-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Lorraine. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:49:42-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi, yeah, good morning. Well, almost afternoon. My name's Stephen Sisson, I'm calling for my mother, it's her house. Our recycling bin is gone."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:49:49-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Gone, okay. Do you mean it didn't get emptied, or the bin itself is missing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:49:54-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "The bin itself. Pickup came, and after that, no bin. I figured the truck took it, but I'm [line breaks up] not sure if that's a thing. Is that a thing?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:03-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You broke up on me a little there. You said the bin disappeared after the pickup, is that right?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:09-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right, right. And this is the second miss in a row. Last time it never got picked up, and now this time the whole bin's gone. So I don't know which is the problem, the pickup or the bin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:21-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, that's two in a row. What's the address?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:24-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "166 Van Zandt Avenue. North End."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:27-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "166 Van Zandt Avenue. And is it the blue recycling bin, or the trash one?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:32-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Um, the recycling. The one with the lid. Or is the trash one the one with the lid? [pause] Sorry, I'm at my mother's and I'm looking at where it used to be. It's the recycling."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:43-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's fine. I'll put in a report for a replacement recycling bin at 166 Van Zandt and note the missed pickup before it. Someone will look at where it went."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:50:52-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. Sorry, one sec, I'm making a list of baby names for a friend, and I've got paper everywhere. Where was I? Do I put anything out in the meantime?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:01-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'd hold the recycling until you have the new bin, or use a sturdy container if you need to put it out. Is a bin sticking out of a box okay? [crosstalk]"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:11-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sorry, [inaudible] say that again? A box?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:14-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I said, if you have to, use a sturdy container of your own and keep it marked as recycling. But the best thing is to wait for the replacement."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:23-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so wait for the new one. Got it, I think. Do you need a number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:28-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:30-05:00",
      "duration": 1,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0172."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:31-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "401-555-0172. Got it, Mr. Sisson. Thanks for calling."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:51:34-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thanks, Lorraine. Take care."
    }
  ],
